| DuckDB persistent secrets are unencrypted on disk by default, and SQL can use available secrets to access external systems. | Securing DuckDB; Secrets Manager | DuckDB | current docs; accessed 2026-09-11 | [security](https://duckdb.org/docs/current/operations_manual/securing_duckdb/overview), [secrets](https://duckdb.org/docs/current/configuration/secrets_manager) | T2 | Security lines 632–635; secrets lines 545–562 | Read-only SQL does not imply non-exfiltration or non-write capability at connected storage. | high |
