**Inference—practical disconfirmation.** Dedicated identities, curated schemas, masking, and read-only grants are necessary controls, not proof of containment. They can fail through role inheritance, owner/bypass behavior, alternate endpoints, copied result sets, logs/transcripts, materialized extracts, broad cloud-storage credentials, and changing policy semantics. The plugin should surface these as explicit evidence gaps, not normalize them into low-confidence passes.

